# DIAGNOSTICS

It prints `nsd: serving /srv/nsd` when it starts.
Without a listen channel it prints `nsd: no listen channel` and exits with `no listen channel`; otherwise it never exits.
Its replies carry statuses, as the calls above say.

# BUGS

`nsd` is not restarted, and its groups would be lost if it were; members would keep resolving with the last text, but binds, mounts and spawns that share would fail.

A group's text is at most 16 KiB; a member whose namespace has grown past that keeps its change to itself.
A member replays the whole text after any change.

A group's connectors are never let go, so a group can take only 8 sources over its life, and a long-lived one stops taking new mounts; nor are a member's connections closed when the text no longer uses them.

`nsd` takes a caller's word: `NSD_TEXT` answers anyone holding `srv:nsd` with any task's namespace, and `NSD_HELLO` takes whatever task id a member claims.

A bad source name in an `NSD_UPDATE` is reported as `NO_MEMORY`, the same as no room.
